{
  "schemaVersion": "northstar.compiler:unbound-permission-acknowledgement/v1",
  "header": [
    "THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Every permission below is declared by the composed application and bound to NO evaluator: every production CurrentPolicyGateway returns ALLOW (program review 2026-08-20, finding R7). Listing a permission here acknowledges that vacuum by name so the release still builds; it does not authorize anything.",
    "An entry leaves when queue row 7 (the policy/identity kernel) binds its permission to an evaluator, or when the permission itself leaves the package. Row 7 empties this list, and when the last entry is gone the refusal is absolute: no declared permission compiles without an evaluator binding.",
    "A permission that is declared and NOT listed refuses the release build by name (COMPILER_PERMISSION_EVALUATOR_UNBOUND). An entry that names a permission the package no longer declares on that resource, or one an evaluator now binds, refuses it too (COMPILER_PERMISSION_ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_STALE) — the list cannot rot. Adding an entry is a deliberate act that a reviewer reads; it is never generated.",
    "Governed packages are exactly the keys of \"packages\". A package not keyed here is ungoverned by this instrument; test/compiler/g2-module-conformance.test.ts pins the composed application as a key and its entries as exactly the declared census, so the key cannot vanish silently."
  ],
